WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:02.208
Now we move from modules and packages

00:00:02.234 --> 00:00:05.776
into the basics of object-oriented programming The

00:00:05.789 --> 00:00:08.829
most important new term is class A

00:00:08.842 --> 00:00:11.960
class is a blueprint It describes what

00:00:11.974 --> 00:00:14.026
information an object should store and what

00:00:14.053 --> 00:00:15.763
actions that object should be able to

00:00:15.789 --> 00:00:18.724
perform Think about a product in an

00:00:18.750 --> 00:00:22.026
analytics system Every product may have a

00:00:22.053 --> 00:00:25.408
name a price and a category A

00:00:25.434 --> 00:00:27.342
product may also need actions such as

00:00:27.368 --> 00:00:30.447
calculating a discounted price or updating inventory

00:00:31.382 --> 00:00:33.092
Instead of storing the data in one

00:00:33.118 --> 00:00:35.276
place and the related functions somewhere else

00:00:35.566 --> 00:00:36.987
a class can keep the data and

00:00:37.013 --> 00:00:40.724
behavior together For example we might define

00:00:40.750 --> 00:00:43.816
a class named Sale The class describes

00:00:43.842 --> 00:00:47.132
what every Sale object should contain After

00:00:47.158 --> 00:00:49.303
defining the class we can create an

00:00:49.316 --> 00:00:52.500
object from that blueprint An object is

00:00:52.526 --> 00:00:55.487
one actual instance If the class is

00:00:55.513 --> 00:00:57.908
Sale one object might represent the sale

00:00:57.921 --> 00:01:00.066
of a notebook while another object might

00:01:00.092 --> 00:01:02.895
represent the sale of a laptop The

00:01:02.921 --> 00:01:05.053
class itself is not the data record

00:01:05.974 --> 00:01:09.158
It is the definition or blueprint The

00:01:09.184 --> 00:01:11.237
objects created from the class hold their

00:01:11.263 --> 00:01:14.263
own values For this course we will

00:01:14.289 --> 00:01:17.290
keep classes simple We will focus on

00:01:17.316 --> 00:01:20.197
attributes which store data and methods which

00:01:20.211 --> 00:01:22.053
perform actions using that data
